# Generated from: specs/438-return-write-spec-to-native-plan-mode-after-merged-publication/requirements.md
Feature: Return write-spec to native plan mode after merged publication
  A queued follow-up containing /plan never dispatched builtin /plan,
  so write-spec continuation stayed in execution mode.

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Merged publication re-enters native plan
    Given the exact materialized merge helper returned merged true for issue 400
    When the execution turn ends terminally
    Then the extension submits /plan and the Continue workflow once through the focused TUI editor
    And plan mode is recorded before the continuation prompt listing published issue 400

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: Continuation keeps plan mode and every published issue
    Given a continuation for issue 400 is running in native plan mode
    When issue 402 is selected, proposed, approved, and published
    Then the next terminal turn end submits a plan-mode continuation listing issues 400 and 402
    And an already-active plan receives the continuation without toggling plan off

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: Fail closed without duplicate or stray submissions
    Given a malformed, unrelated, pre-merge, or duplicate result, a nonterminal turn end, missing UI, an unfocused editor, a non-empty draft, or a submit failure
    When the extension evaluates the continuation
    Then no extra prompt is submitted and any draft is preserved
    And a recorded continuation stays pending with a notification

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: The registered smoke gate can finish a partially delivered queue
    Given a failed smoke invocation delivered issue 7 of queue 7 and 9 with an invocation-bound receipt
    When the same verification is rerun
    Then the provider runs execute for issue 9 only in the retained clone with the same invocation token
    And it passes only after exact-head merged pull requests close issues 7 and 9

  @SCN005 @regression
  Scenario: Execute can resume a queue from a retained clone
    Given the checkout is on the first queued issue's branch or on a delivered issue's branch
    When execute runs a queue
    Then it continues the first issue or leaves the delivered branch for the default branch
    And an undelivered or dirty foreign branch still stops with active_issue_conflict
